{"id": "EUVD-2026-81964", "enisaUuid": "968389ca-0833-3fef-b194-3f79a72538d4", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nARM: 9485/1: mm: acquire mmap write lock around show_pte() for user faults\n\nWhen CONFIG_DEBUG_USER=y, and cmdline \"user_debug=31\" is set,\na user fault may trigger show_pte() without any lock.\nIf another thread in the same process concurrently calls munmap(),\nthe page table pages may be freed while show_pte() is still traversing\nthem, causing a use-after-free in show_pte().\n\nIf CONFIG_ARM_LPAE=y, this may cause a kernel panic if the pages table\nof PMD are freed when show_pte() is running.\n\nAcquire mmap_write_lock() around show_pte() for user faults to fix the\ncontention.\n\nFor user faults, additionally restrict that show_pte() is called only\nwhen the addr is a user-space address (addr < TASK_SIZE). This is because\nthe lock of tsk->mm only protects the virtual memory of user address space,\nfurthermore, dumping the page tables of a kernel-space address for user\nfaults is unnecessary and may have security implications.\n\nKeep everything unchanged for kernel faults, because the kernel is\nalready in the \"oops\" state, acquiring a lock may risk a deadlock.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:08:26", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:01:21", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ab14f07952adfe735d86a53518f8cd576dfd5892", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/07e4d5380f2a844ab7a1b440dde350caf561cbb0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2a14d7797a49a47bccd1a9327fd69da838dcb0dd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/63e3c958a602d0896a101a897c2361878c266ca7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/59bbf86d0ff9373bfa033ca123c1e924f09f1eba", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c71f9a56520b419e55d173052629f2324deb5549", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/720408d98d9fb3c91a12090436734c8c61f04545", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1039bffd6ae9c75b42b7d148d6c1106134107b66"], "aliases": ["GHSA-3rvr-4rpw-5w37", "CVE-2026-90303"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "08747765-8069-35f5-add5-f44a5d257a50", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.270"}, {"id": "20c89802-72ee-3b11-a811-43c8ca7cb4b7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "31e8b7a7-f99a-3063-ae0f-92d31eb51dbe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "600a1173-605e-38bf-b5ed-ea92094be21f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6d021b724481fbb908eb29384898deb9f00dfe70 <c71f9a56520b419e55d173052629f2324deb5549"}, {"id": "6225c5e5-3ef7-3146-a4b4-f68de8ae9fff", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6d021b724481fbb908eb29384898deb9f00dfe70 <63e3c958a602d0896a101a897c2361878c266ca7"}, {"id": "6796d9ba-1af8-3f76-8afe-6f5f1fcc06c5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6d021b724481fbb908eb29384898deb9f00dfe70 <2a14d7797a49a47bccd1a9327fd69da838dcb0dd"}, {"id": "71830eb9-85ac-3b7b-ad53-9f4e606c940c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "7fe0be5f-ec4f-3e73-8596-7905b805b6e9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6d021b724481fbb908eb29384898deb9f00dfe70 <720408d98d9fb3c91a12090436734c8c61f04545"}, {"id": "83a8b519-70fd-3be3-9ab4-16771ad0b1fd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6d021b724481fbb908eb29384898deb9f00dfe70 <ab14f07952adfe735d86a53518f8cd576dfd5892"}, {"id": "88addb6a-2c55-38d0-824a-8bf8f838a153", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "95a96501-44ef-3a7a-921e-7d2f43528ccc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6d021b724481fb